sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Alice's browser
    participant R as Referee server (untrusted)
    participant B as Bob's browser
    Note over A,B: Setup: each browser generates an Ed25519 key, signs a one-time challenge, gets a session
    rect rgba(242,179,61,0.15)
    Note over A,B: Phase 1: COMMIT (moves stay secret)
    A->>A: m_A in {1,2,3}, r_A random, C_A = m_A*G + r_A*H
    A->>A: pi_A = PoK(m_A, r_A) bound to ctx_A, sig_A = Sign(sk_A, ctx_A, C_A, T_A)
    A->>R: POST /commit {C_A, pi_A, sig_A}
    R->>R: verify sig_A + pi_A, store, append to audit log
    B->>B: m_B, r_B, C_B, pi_B, sig_B (same steps)
    B->>R: POST /commit {C_B, pi_B, sig_B}
    R-->>A: WebSocket: both committed, phase = REVEAL (deadline starts)
    R-->>B: WebSocket: phase = REVEAL
    end
    rect rgba(56,211,192,0.15)
    Note over A,B: Phase 2: REVEAL
    A->>A: re-verify sig_B and pi_B locally (don't trust the referee)
    A->>R: POST /reveal {m_A, r_A, Sign(sk_A, ...)}
    B->>B: re-verify sig_A and pi_A locally
    B->>R: POST /reveal {m_B, r_B, Sign(sk_B, ...)}
    R->>R: check m*G + r*H == C for both, judge, log result
    R-->>A: result (tie: new round with fresh commitments)
    R-->>B: result
    A->>A: re-verify Bob's opening locally
    end
    Note over R: No reveal by deadline = forfeit. Wrong opening = forfeit.
